IMPORT prelude

-- Workers Compensation Act 1951 (ACT) -- compensation for an injured private-sector worker.
-- SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE. The rules are written in the Act's own actors and terms: "the worker", "the employer", "the
-- insurer" (a licensed insurer, or the employer as a licensed self-insurer), "the dependants", "the personal
-- representative". The questions are in three seat layers, which IMPORT this module and restate no rule:
-- wca-seat.l4 (the injured worker, and on the worker's death the dependants or personal representative),
-- wca-seat-employer.l4 (the employer) and wca-seat-insurer.l4 (the insurer).
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED. s 20 (cpi indexing and the no-negative-adjustment rule); s 36G (initial incapacity date,
-- pension age, statutory floor); s 37; s 38; ss 39-42; ss 43, 43A, 43B (through the week's facts); ss 44, 45; s 83
-- (as a fact, because s 43B counts it); ss 48-51, 53-57, 59, 61 and Schedule 1 (all 54 items); s 77 and its
-- dictionary terms (dependant, child, full-time student); s 93, s 94(2)-(3), s 95; s 116(2), s 118(2), s 119;
-- s 120(1)-(2); s 121; s 122; s 126(1); s 127(2); ss 128-132; s 134.
-- Duties and deadlines are regulative rules (DEONTIC); amounts and dates are functions.
--
-- FIGURES. The Act's own base figures are encoded: the single loss amount $100 000 (s 49) and the maximum loss amount
-- $150 000 (s 50), both cpi indexed; the death lump sum $539 002.37 and the weekly payment for a dependent child
-- $148.23, both wpi indexed, and the funeral expenses maximum $11 828.87 cpi indexed (s 77(2)). The indexed values
-- current in October 2026 are NOT in the deposit (no Workers Compensation Regulation 2002 or indexation notice is
-- deposited), so every question takes the indexed amount, the AWE, the statutory floor and the index numbers as
-- INPUTS. The index arithmetic of s 20 and s 77(7) is encoded so that an index number can be turned into an amount.
--
-- Edition: Workers Compensation Act 1951 (A1951-2), Republication No 88, effective 26 November 2025, as deposited
-- at ../../registers/source-bundle/A1951-2.txt (converted from the register's unauthorised DOCX).
--
-- BASELINE. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, design defaults of 2026-10-18.
-- No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice.
-- See NOTES.md.

§ `Workers Compensation Act 1951 (ACT) -- seat-neutral core`

§§ `Dates`

-- The Act counts in days, weeks and years. "N days after" a day is read as the day N days later (the day itself
-- excluded, as the Legislation Act 2001 s 151 does; that Act is not deposited). "N years after" a day is the same
-- date N years later; READING: from 29 February to a year without one, 28 February.
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`days after` `n` `the day` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS `n`)

GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a leap year` `the year` IF
        ((`the year` MODULO 4) EQUALS 0 AND (NOT ((`the year` MODULO 100) EQUALS 0)))
    OR  (`the year` MODULO 400) EQUALS 0

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`years after` `n` `the day` MEANS
    IF      DATE_DAY `the day` EQUALS 29
        AND DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 2
        AND (NOT (`is a leap year` (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS `n`)))
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS `n`)
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY (DATE_DAY `the day`) (DATE_MONTH `the day`) (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS `n`)

GIVEN `the earlier day` IS A DATE, `the later day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days from` `the earlier day` `to` `the later day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the later day` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the earlier day`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a` `is on or before` `b` IF DATE_SERIAL `a` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `b`

§§ `20 and 77(7) -- cpi indexed and wpi indexed amounts`

-- s 20(1): "cpi indexed, for an amount, means the amount as adjusted in line with any adjustment in the CPI since the
-- commencement of the provision in which the amount appears" (CPI: All Groups Consumer Price Index (Canberra)).
-- s 20(2): an amount to be awe or cpi indexed "is not reduced in line with the negative adjustment"; (3)-(4): a later
-- increase counts only so far as it does not cancel out the negative adjustment. The s 20 example: $100; CPI +20% gives
-- $120; CPI -10% leaves $120 (not $108); CPI +20% again gives $129.60 (20% on the $108).
-- READING: the effect of (2)-(4) is that the amount is the Act's figure times the HIGHEST ratio the index has reached
-- since commencement, and never less than the figure itself (the s 20 example is asserted on this reading).
GIVEN `the figure in the Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the index number when the provision commenced` IS A NUMBER
      `the highest index number since then` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the cpi indexed amount` `the figure in the Act` `the index number when the provision commenced` `the highest index number since then` MEANS
    `the figure in the Act` TIMES (max 1 (`the highest index number since then` DIVIDED BY `the index number when the provision commenced`))

-- s 77(7): "wpi indexed, for an amount, means the amount as adjusted in line with any adjustment in the WPI since the
-- commencement of the provision in which the amount appears" (WPI: the Wage Price Index number published by the
-- Australian Statistician). s 20(2)-(4) speak only of an amount "to be awe indexed or cpi indexed", so the
-- no-negative rule does not reach a wpi indexed amount: read literally, it follows the latest WPI down as well as up.
GIVEN `the figure in the Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the index number when the provision commenced` IS A NUMBER
      `the latest index number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the wpi indexed amount` `the figure in the Act` `the index number when the provision commenced` `the latest index number` MEANS
    `the figure in the Act` TIMES `the latest index number` DIVIDED BY `the index number when the provision commenced`

-- The indexed figures of the Act. Each provision's commencement, from the endnotes of the republication: ss 49 and 50
-- were inserted by A2001-81 s 11, commenced 1 July 2002; s 77 was amended by A2017-49 ss 9-11, commenced
-- 13 December 2017 (the figures in s 77(2) and (6) are taken to date from then; the endnotes do not say which
-- amendment wrote each figure).
DECLARE `Indexed figure` IS ONE OF
    `the single loss amount (s 49)`
    `the maximum loss amount (s 50)`
    `the funeral expenses maximum (s 77(2)(c), (6))`
    `the death lump sum (s 77(2)(a))`
    `the weekly payment for each dependent child (s 77(2)(b))`

DECLARE `Index` IS ONE OF `the CPI (Canberra)`, `the WPI`

GIVEN `the figure` IS AN `Indexed figure`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the figure in the Act for` `the figure` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the figure`
    WHEN `the single loss amount (s 49)` THEN 100000
    WHEN `the maximum loss amount (s 50)` THEN 150000
    WHEN `the funeral expenses maximum (s 77(2)(c), (6))` THEN 11828.87
    WHEN `the death lump sum (s 77(2)(a))` THEN 539002.37
    WHEN `the weekly payment for each dependent child (s 77(2)(b))` THEN 148.23

GIVEN `the figure` IS AN `Indexed figure`
GIVETH AN `Index`
`the index for` `the figure` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the figure`
    WHEN `the death lump sum (s 77(2)(a))` THEN `the WPI`
    WHEN `the weekly payment for each dependent child (s 77(2)(b))` THEN `the WPI`
    OTHERWISE `the CPI (Canberra)`

§§ `36G -- definitions for weekly compensation`

-- s 36G(1): initial incapacity date: "the date the worker first becomes incapacitated (whether totally or partially)
-- for work because of the injury". pension age: "the meaning given by the Social Security Act 1991 (Cwlth), section 23
-- (5A), (5B), (5C) and (5D)" -- an INPUT, as the day the worker reaches it. statutory floor: "the national minimum
-- wage set by a national minimum wage order in an annual wage review by the Fair Work Commission under the Fair Work
-- Act 2009 (Cwlth)" -- an INPUT, as a weekly amount. s 41(2): pre-incapacity floor: "the statutory floor that applied
-- immediately before the initial incapacity date". s 42(4): statutory ceiling: "150% of AWE at the time the amount is
-- to be paid". AWE (dictionary): ACT average weekly earnings, seasonally adjusted, all males total earnings, from the
-- ABS -- an INPUT.
-- ss 6, 7, 35: totally incapacitated (no suitable paid employment reasonably available that the worker can do because
-- of the injury, or taken to be under s 35); partially incapacitated (cannot do all the work the worker could do
-- before, and not totally incapacitated). Which one applies is a fact for this encoding.
DECLARE `Incapacity` IS ONE OF
    `totally incapacitated for work`
    `partially incapacitated for work`
    `not incapacitated for work`

GIVEN `AWE at the time of payment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the statutory ceiling` `AWE at the time of payment` MEANS 150% TIMES `AWE at the time of payment`

-- The facts for one week of weekly compensation. s 21-24: average pre-incapacity weekly earnings and hours are worked
-- out from the year before the injury (or from comparable workers); they are INPUTS here.
DECLARE `Weekly facts` HAS
    `the day asked about`                                           IS A DATE
    `the initial incapacity date`                                   IS A DATE     -- s 36G(1)
    `the day the worker reaches pension age`                        IS A DATE     -- s 36G(1); Social Security Act s 23
    `the worker is`                                                 IS AN `Incapacity`
    `average pre-incapacity weekly earnings`                        IS A NUMBER   -- ss 21, 22, 25, 26
    `average pre-incapacity weekly hours`                           IS A NUMBER   -- ss 23, 24, 25, 26
    `the weekly amount the worker is paid for working or could earn in reasonably available suitable employment` IS A NUMBER  -- s 39(4)(b)(ii), (5); s 42(1), (3)
    `the hours a week the worker is working`                        IS A NUMBER   -- s 42(2)
    `weeks of weekly compensation already counted under s 39`       IS A NUMBER   -- s 39(3)(a), s 40(1)(b), s 43B
    `the statutory floor at the time of payment`                    IS A NUMBER   -- s 36G
    `the pre-incapacity floor`                                      IS A NUMBER   -- s 41(2)
    `AWE at the time of payment`                                    IS A NUMBER   -- s 42(4)
    `the worker is dead`                                            IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 37
    `the worker has stopped living in Australia`                    IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 44(1)
    `the incapacity is likely to be permanent`                      IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 44(2)(a)
    `the absence from Australia is likely to help the worker recuperate` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 44(2)(b)
    `the worker proves identity and continuing incapacity`          IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 45(3)
    `the worker is imprisoned after a conviction`                   IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 83

§§ `39, 40 -- the age limits`

-- s 39(3), and the same words in s 40(4): the worker is not entitled
--   "(b) if the worker was, on the initial incapacity date for the injury, younger than the pension age by more than
--   2 years--for any period after the worker reaches pension age; or (c) if ... younger than the pension age by 2 years
--   or less--for any period more than 2 years after the initial incapacity date; or (d) if ... pension age or older--
--   for any period more than 2 years after the initial incapacity date."
-- (c) and (d) give the same answer. READING: "after the worker reaches pension age" excludes the day pension age is
-- reached; "more than 2 years after" keeps the second anniversary of the initial incapacity date.
DECLARE `Age limit` IS ONE OF
    `no weekly compensation from the day the worker reaches pension age` HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `no weekly compensation for any day after the second anniversary of the initial incapacity date` HAS `the anniversary` IS A DATE

GIVEN `the initial incapacity date` IS A DATE
      `the day the worker reaches pension age` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Age limit`
`the age limit for` `the initial incapacity date` `the day the worker reaches pension age` MEANS
    IF DATE_SERIAL `the day the worker reaches pension age` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL (`years after` 2 `the initial incapacity date`)
    THEN `no weekly compensation from the day the worker reaches pension age` `the day the worker reaches pension age`
    ELSE `no weekly compensation for any day after the second anniversary of the initial incapacity date` (`years after` 2 `the initial incapacity date`)

GIVEN `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `the limit` IS AN `Age limit`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the age limit has passed on` `the day asked about` `the limit` IF
    CONSIDER `the limit`
    WHEN `no weekly compensation from the day the worker reaches pension age` `the day` THEN DATE_SERIAL `the day asked about` AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL `the day`
    WHEN `no weekly compensation for any day after the second anniversary of the initial incapacity date` `the anniversary` THEN DATE_SERIAL `the day asked about` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `the anniversary`

§§ `39 -- the first 26 weeks`

-- s 39(3)(a): no weekly compensation under s 39 "for a period of longer than, or for periods (whether or not
-- continuous) totalling more than, 26 weeks". s 43B: a period stopped under s 83 or s 113 counts towards the 26 weeks.
-- s 39(4): "(a) for any period during which the person is totally incapacitated ...--the worker's average
-- pre-incapacity weekly earnings; (b) for any period during which the person is partially incapacitated ...--the
-- difference between--(i) the worker's average pre-incapacity weekly earnings; and (ii) the average weekly amount that
-- the worker is being paid for working or could earn in reasonably available suitable employment."
-- READING: "the difference" is the earnings less the amount paid or available, and never below nil.
`the weeks of weekly compensation under s 39` MEANS 26

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Weekly facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the week falls in the first 26 weeks` `the facts` IF
    `the facts`'s `weeks of weekly compensation already counted under s 39` LESS THAN `the weeks of weekly compensation under s 39`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Weekly facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 39 weekly amount` `the facts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the facts`'s `the worker is`
    WHEN `totally incapacitated for work` THEN `the facts`'s `average pre-incapacity weekly earnings`
    WHEN `partially incapacitated for work` THEN
        max 0 (`the facts`'s `average pre-incapacity weekly earnings` MINUS `the facts`'s `the weekly amount the worker is paid for working or could earn in reasonably available suitable employment`)
    WHEN `not incapacitated for work` THEN 0

§§ `41 -- after 26 weeks of total incapacity`

-- s 41(1): weekly compensation equal to "(a) if 100% of the worker's average pre-incapacity weekly earnings is less
-- than the pre-incapacity floor ...--100% of the worker's average pre-incapacity weekly earnings; or (b) if 100% of the
-- worker's average pre-incapacity weekly earnings is more, but 65% of those earnings is less, than the pre-incapacity
-- floor ...--the statutory floor; or (c) if 65% of the worker's average pre-incapacity weekly earnings is more than the
-- pre-incapacity floor ...--whichever of the following is (at the time of payment) more: (i) 65% of the worker's
-- average pre-incapacity weekly earnings; (ii) the statutory floor."
-- No paragraph applies where the earnings, or 65% of them, EQUAL the pre-incapacity floor: not covered, asserted.
DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `s 41(1) says nothing where 100% or 65% of the earnings equals the pre-incapacity floor`
    `the item is not one of the 54 items of Schedule 1`
    `a claim for an imminently fatal asbestos-related disease (ss 116(2)(a), 121(2)(a), 122(1)(a), 128A) is outside this encoding`

DECLARE `Weekly amount` IS ONE OF
    `the weekly amount is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER, `under` IS A STRING
    `the weekly amount is not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

GIVEN `the earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the pre-incapacity floor` IS A NUMBER
      `the statutory floor` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Weekly amount`
`the s 41 weekly amount` `the earnings` `the pre-incapacity floor` `the statutory floor` MEANS
    IF `the earnings` LESS THAN `the pre-incapacity floor`
    THEN `the weekly amount is` `the earnings` "s 41(1)(a)"
    ELSE IF `the earnings` GREATER THAN `the pre-incapacity floor` AND (65% TIMES `the earnings`) LESS THAN `the pre-incapacity floor`
         THEN `the weekly amount is` `the statutory floor` "s 41(1)(b)"
         ELSE IF (65% TIMES `the earnings`) GREATER THAN `the pre-incapacity floor`
              THEN `the weekly amount is` (max (65% TIMES `the earnings`) `the statutory floor`) "s 41(1)(c)"
              ELSE `the weekly amount is not covered` `s 41(1) says nothing where 100% or 65% of the earnings equals the pre-incapacity floor`

§§ `42 -- after 26 weeks of partial incapacity`

-- s 42(2): the relevant percentage is "(a) if the worker is not working or works 25% of the worker's average
-- pre-incapacity weekly hours or less--65%; (b) ... more than 25% ... but not more than 50%--75%; (c) ... more than 50%
-- ... but not more than 75%--85%; (d) ... more than 75% ... but not more than 85%--95%; (e) ... more than 85%--100%."
GIVEN `the hours a week the worker is working` IS A NUMBER
      `average pre-incapacity weekly hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the relevant percentage` `the hours a week the worker is working` `average pre-incapacity weekly hours` MEANS
    IF `the hours a week the worker is working` AT MOST 0 OR `average pre-incapacity weekly hours` AT MOST 0
    THEN 65%
    ELSE BRANCH
            IF `the share of hours` AT MOST 25% THEN 65%
            IF `the share of hours` AT MOST 50% THEN 75%
            IF `the share of hours` AT MOST 75% THEN 85%
            IF `the share of hours` AT MOST 85% THEN 95%
            OTHERWISE 100%
    WHERE
        `the share of hours` MEANS `the hours a week the worker is working` DIVIDED BY `average pre-incapacity weekly hours`

-- s 42(1): weekly compensation "equal to the difference between the weekly amount the worker is being paid for
-- working or could earn in reasonably available suitable employment and--(a) if 100% of the worker's average
-- pre-incapacity weekly earnings is less than the statutory floor--100% of the worker's average pre-incapacity weekly
-- earnings; or (b) if the relevant percentage of the worker's average pre-incapacity weekly earnings is less than the
-- statutory floor--the statutory floor; or (c) if the relevant percentage ... is more than the statutory ceiling--the
-- statutory ceiling; or (d) in any other case--the relevant percentage of the worker's average pre-incapacity weekly
-- earnings." (a) and (b) overlap whenever (a) applies; READING: the paragraphs are taken in order, so (a) wins.
-- READING, as in s 39: the difference is never below nil.
-- Note that s 42 compares with the statutory floor at the time of payment, where s 41 uses the pre-incapacity floor.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Weekly facts`
GIVETH A `Weekly amount`
`the s 42 weekly amount` `the facts` MEANS
    IF `the earnings` LESS THAN `the floor`
    THEN `the weekly amount is` (`less what is earned` `the earnings`) "s 42(1)(a)"
    ELSE IF `the relevant share of the earnings` LESS THAN `the floor`
         THEN `the weekly amount is` (`less what is earned` `the floor`) "s 42(1)(b)"
         ELSE IF `the relevant share of the earnings` GREATER THAN `the ceiling`
              THEN `the weekly amount is` (`less what is earned` `the ceiling`) "s 42(1)(c)"
              ELSE `the weekly amount is` (`less what is earned` `the relevant share of the earnings`) "s 42(1)(d)"
    WHERE
        `the earnings` MEANS `the facts`'s `average pre-incapacity weekly earnings`
        `the floor` MEANS `the facts`'s `the statutory floor at the time of payment`
        `the ceiling` MEANS `the statutory ceiling` (`the facts`'s `AWE at the time of payment`)
        `the relevant share of the earnings` MEANS
            `the relevant percentage` (`the facts`'s `the hours a week the worker is working`) (`the facts`'s `average pre-incapacity weekly hours`) TIMES `the earnings`
        GIVEN `the amount` IS A NUMBER
        `less what is earned` `the amount` MEANS
            max 0 (`the amount` MINUS `the facts`'s `the weekly amount the worker is paid for working or could earn in reasonably available suitable employment`)

§§ `37, 39-45, 83 -- weekly compensation for a week`

-- s 40: after the worker has received 26 weeks under s 39, s 41 applies to total incapacity and s 42 to partial.
-- s 43(1), s 43A(1): weekly compensation stops when the worker stops being totally (or partially) incapacitated,
-- returns to work (total incapacity) or dies; s 43(2), s 43A(2): it starts again if the incapacity returns. Here the
-- week's incapacity is a fact, so a week without incapacity pays nothing and a later week with it pays again.
-- s 37: "A worker is not entitled to weekly compensation if the worker is dead", apart from what accrued before.
-- s 83: no compensation "for a period when the worker is imprisoned because the worker has been convicted of an
-- offence". s 44(1): no weekly compensation "if the worker stops living in Australia", unless (2) "(a) the incapacity
-- resulting from the injury is likely to be permanent; or (b) the worker's absence from Australia is likely to help
-- the worker recuperate". s 45(2): a worker still entitled while living outside Australia "is entitled to receive
-- quarterly the amount of the weekly compensation payable during the previous quarter", and (3) only on proving
-- identity and continuing incapacity.
DECLARE `Why no weekly compensation` IS ONE OF
    `the worker is dead (s 37), apart from weekly compensation that accrued before death`
    `the worker is imprisoned after a conviction (s 83)`
    `the worker has stopped living in Australia (s 44(1))`
    `the worker lives outside Australia and has not proved identity and continuing incapacity (s 45(3))`
    `the age limit in s 39(3) and s 40(4) has passed`
    `the worker is not incapacitated for work because of the injury`

DECLARE `Weekly compensation` IS ONE OF
    `weekly compensation, in dollars a week` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER, `under` IS A STRING
    `paid quarterly while living outside Australia (s 45), in dollars a week` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER, `under` IS A STRING
    `no weekly compensation` HAS `because` IS A `Why no weekly compensation`
    `weekly compensation not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Weekly facts`
GIVETH A `Weekly amount`
`the weekly amount under ss 39 to 42` `the facts` MEANS
    IF `the week falls in the first 26 weeks` `the facts`
    THEN CONSIDER `the facts`'s `the worker is`
         WHEN `totally incapacitated for work` THEN `the weekly amount is` (`the s 39 weekly amount` `the facts`) "s 39(4)(a)"
         OTHERWISE `the weekly amount is` (`the s 39 weekly amount` `the facts`) "s 39(4)(b)"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the facts`'s `the worker is`
         WHEN `totally incapacitated for work` THEN
             `the s 41 weekly amount` (`the facts`'s `average pre-incapacity weekly earnings`) (`the facts`'s `the pre-incapacity floor`) (`the facts`'s `the statutory floor at the time of payment`)
         OTHERWISE `the s 42 weekly amount` `the facts`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Weekly facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the worker keeps weekly compensation outside Australia` `the facts` IF
        `the facts`'s `the incapacity is likely to be permanent`
    OR  `the facts`'s `the absence from Australia is likely to help the worker recuperate`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Weekly facts`
GIVETH A `Weekly compensation`
`the weekly compensation for` `the facts` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facts`'s `the worker is dead`
            THEN `no weekly compensation` `the worker is dead (s 37), apart from weekly compensation that accrued before death`
        IF `the facts`'s `the worker is imprisoned after a conviction`
            THEN `no weekly compensation` `the worker is imprisoned after a conviction (s 83)`
        IF `the facts`'s `the worker has stopped living in Australia` AND (NOT (`the worker keeps weekly compensation outside Australia` `the facts`))
            THEN `no weekly compensation` `the worker has stopped living in Australia (s 44(1))`
        IF `the age limit has passed on` (`the facts`'s `the day asked about`) (`the age limit for` (`the facts`'s `the initial incapacity date`) (`the facts`'s `the day the worker reaches pension age`))
            THEN `no weekly compensation` `the age limit in s 39(3) and s 40(4) has passed`
        IF `the facts`'s `the worker is` EQUALS `not incapacitated for work`
            THEN `no weekly compensation` `the worker is not incapacitated for work because of the injury`
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the weekly amount under ss 39 to 42` `the facts`
            WHEN `the weekly amount is not covered` `why` THEN `weekly compensation not covered` `why`
            WHEN `the weekly amount is` `dollars` `under` THEN
                IF `the facts`'s `the worker has stopped living in Australia`
                THEN IF `the facts`'s `the worker proves identity and continuing incapacity`
                     THEN `paid quarterly while living outside Australia (s 45), in dollars a week` `dollars` `under`
                     ELSE `no weekly compensation` `the worker lives outside Australia and has not proved identity and continuing incapacity (s 45(3))`
                ELSE `weekly compensation, in dollars a week` `dollars` `under`

§§ `38 -- weekly payments begin on notice, and a claim within 7 days keeps them going`

-- s 38(1): "(a) the payment of weekly compensation must begin when the worker gives notice of the injury to the
-- employer; and (b) the worker is or may be entitled to weekly compensation from the date of the injury."
-- s 38(2): "if, at the end of 7 days after the date of the injury, the worker has not made a claim for compensation--
-- (a) payment of weekly compensation ends; and (b) the worker is not entitled to weekly compensation for the injury for
-- the period--(i) beginning on the day 8 days after the date of the injury; and (ii) ending on the day before the day
-- the worker makes a claim for the injury."
-- s 38(3): (2) does not apply if "(a) the worker cannot make a claim before the end of the 7-day period because of the
-- injury; and (b) the worker makes the claim not later than 7 days after the day the worker is first able to make the
-- claim."
-- So a claim made on the 8th day after the injury loses no day: the lost period would begin and end on the same
-- boundary and is empty.
`the days to claim under s 38(2)` MEANS 7

GIVEN `the date of the injury` IS A DATE
      `the injury prevented a claim within the 7 days` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the worker was first able to claim` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to claim and keep weekly payments going` `the date of the injury` `the injury prevented a claim within the 7 days` `the day the worker was first able to claim` MEANS
    IF `the injury prevented a claim within the 7 days`
    THEN `days after` `the days to claim under s 38(2)` `the day the worker was first able to claim`
    ELSE `days after` `the days to claim under s 38(2)` `the date of the injury`

DECLARE `Late claim` IS ONE OF
    `no weekly compensation is lost under s 38(2)`
    `no weekly compensation for the days` HAS `from` IS A DATE, `to` IS A DATE

GIVEN `the date of the injury` IS A DATE
      `the day the claim is made` IS A DATE
      `the injury prevented a claim within the 7 days` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the worker was first able to claim` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Late claim`
`the days lost for a late claim` `the date of the injury` `the day the claim is made` `the injury prevented a claim within the 7 days` `the day the worker was first able to claim` MEANS
    IF      `the day the claim is made` `is on or before` (`days after` `the days to claim under s 38(2)` `the date of the injury`)
        OR  (`the injury prevented a claim within the 7 days` AND (`the day the claim is made` `is on or before` (`days after` `the days to claim under s 38(2)` `the day the worker was first able to claim`)))
        OR  `the day the claim is made` `is on or before` (`days after` 8 `the date of the injury`)
    THEN `no weekly compensation is lost under s 38(2)`
    ELSE `no weekly compensation for the days` (`days after` 8 `the date of the injury`) (`days after` (0 MINUS 1) `the day the claim is made`)

§§ `48-61 and Schedule 1 -- lump sums for permanent injuries`

-- s 51(1): a worker who has suffered a loss mentioned in an item of schedule 1 "is entitled to receive from the
-- worker's employer, as compensation for the loss, the percentage of the single loss amount mentioned in that item".
-- s 49: single loss amount "$100 000 cpi indexed". s 50: maximum loss amount "$150 000 cpi indexed".
-- s 48: loss includes the loss of the thing, the permanent loss of its use or efficient use, permanent impairment, and
-- anything in schedule 1. s 51(2): the loss is worked out when the employer became liable and no further improvement
-- is likely -- the assessed loss is an INPUT here.
-- Schedule 1, column 3: "% of single loss amount payable". All 54 items.
DECLARE `Schedule 1 item` HAS
    `item`                              IS A NUMBER
    `nature of injury`                  IS A STRING
    `percent of the single loss amount` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `nature` IS A STRING, `percent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Schedule 1 item`
`item` `n` `nature` `percent` MEANS
    `Schedule 1 item` WITH
        `item`                              IS `n`
        `nature of injury`                  IS `nature`
        `percent of the single loss amount` IS `percent`

`Schedule 1` MEANS LIST
    `item` 1  "loss of power of speech" 60,
    `item` 2  "loss of sense of taste or smell" 17,
    `item` 3  "loss of senses of taste and smell" 34,
    `item` 4  "loss of hearing of both ears" 65,
    `item` 5  "loss of hearing of 1 ear" 20,
    `item` 6  "loss of sight of both eyes" 100,
    `item` 7  "loss of sight of an only eye" 100,
    `item` 8  "loss of sight of 1 eye, together with serious diminution of the sight of the other eye" 75,
    `item` 9  "loss of sight of 1 eye" 40,
    `item` 10 "loss of binocular vision (if not otherwise compensable under this schedule)" 40,
    `item` 11 "loss of eyeball (in addition to compensation for loss of sight of the eye)" 22,
    `item` 12 "loss of right arm at or above elbow" 80,
    `item` 13 "loss of right arm below elbow" 75,
    `item` 14 "loss of left arm at or above elbow" 75,
    `item` 15 "loss of left arm below elbow" 70,
    `item` 16 "loss of right hand" 70,
    `item` 17 "loss of left hand" 65,
    `item` 18 "loss of thumb of right hand" 30,
    `item` 19 "loss of thumb of left hand" 26,
    `item` 20 "loss of a joint of thumb" 16,
    `item` 21 "loss of forefinger of right hand" 21,
    `item` 22 "loss of forefinger of left hand" 18,
    `item` 23 "loss of 2 joints of forefinger of right hand" 16,
    `item` 24 "loss of 2 joints of forefinger of left hand" 12,
    `item` 25 "loss of first joint of forefinger of right hand" 10,
    `item` 26 "loss of first joint of forefinger of left hand" 9,
    `item` 27 "loss of middle finger of either hand" 12,
    `item` 28 "loss of 2 joints of middle finger of either hand" 10,
    `item` 29 "loss of first joint of middle finger of either hand" 6,
    `item` 30 "loss of little or ring finger of either hand" 11,
    `item` 31 "loss of 2 joints of little or ring finger of either hand" 9,
    `item` 32 "loss of first joint of little or ring finger of either hand" 6,
    `item` 33 "loss of either leg at or above knee" 75,
    `item` 34 "loss of either leg below knee" 70,
    `item` 35 "loss of a foot" 65,
    `item` 36 "loss of great toe of either foot" 22,
    `item` 37 "loss of a joint of great toe of either foot" 10,
    `item` 38 "loss of any other toe" 6,
    `item` 39 "loss of any joint of any other toe" 2,
    `item` 40 "permanent loss of bowel function" 65,
    `item` 41 "loss of sexual organs" 47,
    `item` 42 "loss of both breasts" 47,
    `item` 43 "loss of 1 breast" 30,
    `item` 44 "permanent and total loss of capacity to engage in sexual intercourse" 75,
    `item` 45 "permanent brain damage if not, or not completely an injury otherwise compensable under this schedule" 100,
    `item` 46 "permanent impairment of back" 60,
    `item` 47 "permanent impairment of neck" 40,
    `item` 48 "permanent impairment of pelvis" 15,
    `item` 49 "severe facial disfigurement if not, or not completely, an injury otherwise compensable under this schedule" 80,
    `item` 50 "severe bodily disfigurement if not, or not completely, an injury otherwise compensable under this schedule" 50,
    `item` 51 "HIV infection (Human Immunodeficiency Virus infection)" 100,
    `item` 52 "AIDS (Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome)" 100,
    `item` 53 "imminently fatal asbestos-related disease" 100,
    `item` 54 "silicosis" 100

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Schedule 1 item`
`the Schedule 1 item numbered` `n` MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN `row` YIELD `row`'s `item` EQUALS `n`) `Schedule 1`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `found` FOLLOWED BY `others` THEN JUST `found`

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Schedule 1 percentage of item` `n` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Schedule 1 item numbered` `n`
    WHEN JUST `row` THEN `row`'s `percent of the single loss amount`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0

-- s 54: "If a worker's left arm or hand is the worker's dominant limb ... (a) the loss of the worker's left arm, left
-- hand or fingers of left hand is to be compensated as if it is the loss of the worker's right arm, right hand or
-- fingers of right hand; and (b) [the reverse]." The right and left pairs in Schedule 1: items 12/14, 13/15, 16/17,
-- 18/19, 21/22, 23/24, 25/26. (Items 20 and 27-32 do not distinguish the hands.)
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER
      `the worker's left arm or hand is dominant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the item compensated under s 54` `n` `the worker's left arm or hand is dominant` MEANS
    IF `the worker's left arm or hand is dominant`
    THEN CONSIDER `n`
         WHEN 12 THEN 14
         WHEN 14 THEN 12
         WHEN 13 THEN 15
         WHEN 15 THEN 13
         WHEN 16 THEN 17
         WHEN 17 THEN 16
         WHEN 18 THEN 19
         WHEN 19 THEN 18
         WHEN 21 THEN 22
         WHEN 22 THEN 21
         WHEN 23 THEN 24
         WHEN 24 THEN 23
         WHEN 25 THEN 26
         WHEN 26 THEN 25
         OTHERWISE `n`
    ELSE `n`

-- s 56: "Loss of an only arm, leg, hand or foot is treated under schedule 1 as the loss of both arms, legs, hands or
-- feet." Schedule 1 has no item for both arms, both legs, both hands or both feet. READING: the loss of both is the two
-- items together (right and left arm at the same level; the leg item twice; right and left hand; the foot item twice),
-- which s 53 then caps at the maximum loss amount. Returns NOTHING for an item that is not an arm, leg, hand or foot.
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the s 56 percentage for an only limb` `n` MEANS
    CONSIDER `n`
    WHEN 12 THEN JUST (`the Schedule 1 percentage of item` 12 PLUS `the Schedule 1 percentage of item` 14)
    WHEN 14 THEN JUST (`the Schedule 1 percentage of item` 12 PLUS `the Schedule 1 percentage of item` 14)
    WHEN 13 THEN JUST (`the Schedule 1 percentage of item` 13 PLUS `the Schedule 1 percentage of item` 15)
    WHEN 15 THEN JUST (`the Schedule 1 percentage of item` 13 PLUS `the Schedule 1 percentage of item` 15)
    WHEN 16 THEN JUST (`the Schedule 1 percentage of item` 16 PLUS `the Schedule 1 percentage of item` 17)
    WHEN 17 THEN JUST (`the Schedule 1 percentage of item` 16 PLUS `the Schedule 1 percentage of item` 17)
    WHEN 33 THEN JUST (2 TIMES `the Schedule 1 percentage of item` 33)
    WHEN 34 THEN JUST (2 TIMES `the Schedule 1 percentage of item` 34)
    WHEN 35 THEN JUST (2 TIMES `the Schedule 1 percentage of item` 35)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 57: "(subject to the maximum percentage of 47% and without limiting compensation for the loss of another sexual
-- organ): (a) the percentage payable for loss of the penis is 47%; (b) the percentage payable for loss of 1 testicle is
-- 10%; (c) the percentage payable for loss of 2 testicles or an only testicle is 47%."
-- READING: for item 41, where the penis or a testicle is lost, the percentage is the s 57 figures added and capped at
-- 47; where another sexual organ is lost, it is item 41's 47.
DECLARE `Sexual organ losses` HAS
    `the penis is lost`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of testicles lost, an only testicle counting as 2` IS A NUMBER

`the s 57 maximum percentage` MEANS 47

GIVEN `the losses` IS A `Sexual organ losses`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 57 percentage` `the losses` MEANS
    min `the s 57 maximum percentage` (`for the penis` PLUS `for the testicles`)
    WHERE
        `for the penis` MEANS IF `the losses`'s `the penis is lost` THEN 47 ELSE 0
        `for the testicles` MEANS
            IF `the losses`'s `the number of testicles lost, an only testicle counting as 2` AT LEAST 2
            THEN 47
            ELSE IF `the losses`'s `the number of testicles lost, an only testicle counting as 2` EQUALS 1
                 THEN 10
                 ELSE 0

-- s 59(1): where the loss is "of a proportion, but not all, of a thing mentioned in schedule 1", the compensation is
-- "a percentage of the compensation payable for the total loss of the thing equal to the percentage lost". (2): an
-- external removable aid is not taken into account; (3): the amount is worked out by agreement, conciliation or
-- arbitration -- so the proportion lost is an INPUT.
-- s 61(1): "an amount must be deducted from the compensation (the deductible proportion) for any proportion of the loss
-- attributable to--(a) a previous injury ...; or (b) a pre-existing condition or abnormality." (3): if the deductible
-- proportion "will be difficult or costly to work out, it is to be assumed that the deductible proportion for the loss
-- ... is 10% of the loss, unless this assumption is contrary to the available evidence". The s 61 example: a loss of
-- 30% of the use of the right arm with the 10% assumption has a deductible proportion of 3% (10% of 30%).
-- s 55: a loss that a combination of items or a proportion of one item could compensate is compensated as a proportion
-- of the single item; the assessed item and proportion are INPUTS, so s 55 is applied before the facts are stated.
DECLARE `Permanent loss` HAS
    `the Schedule 1 item`                                              IS A NUMBER   -- s 51, Schedule 1
    `the percentage of the thing lost`                                 IS A NUMBER   -- s 59: 100 for a total loss
    `the deductible proportion, as a percentage of the loss`           IS A NUMBER   -- s 61(1): 0 if none
    `the deductible proportion is difficult or costly to work out`     IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 61(3)
    `it is the worker's only arm, leg, hand or foot`                   IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 56

`the s 61(3) assumed deductible proportion` MEANS 10

GIVEN `the loss` IS A `Permanent loss`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deductible proportion under s 61` `the loss` MEANS
    IF `the loss`'s `the deductible proportion is difficult or costly to work out`
    THEN `the s 61(3) assumed deductible proportion`
    ELSE `the loss`'s `the deductible proportion, as a percentage of the loss`

-- The percentage of the single loss amount for one loss: the Schedule 1 percentage (with s 54, s 56 and s 57), times
-- the percentage of the thing lost (s 59), less the deductible proportion (s 61). NOTHING if the item is not in
-- Schedule 1.
GIVEN `the loss` IS A `Permanent loss`
      `the worker's left arm or hand is dominant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sexual organ losses` IS A `Sexual organ losses`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the percentage of the single loss amount for` `the loss` `the worker's left arm or hand is dominant` `the sexual organ losses` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Schedule 1 item numbered` (`the loss`'s `the Schedule 1 item`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `row` THEN
        JUST (`the item percentage` TIMES (`the loss`'s `the percentage of the thing lost`) DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES (100 MINUS `the deductible proportion under s 61` `the loss`) DIVIDED BY 100)
    WHERE
        `the item percentage` MEANS
            IF `the loss`'s `it is the worker's only arm, leg, hand or foot`
            THEN CONSIDER `the s 56 percentage for an only limb` (`the loss`'s `the Schedule 1 item`)
                 WHEN JUST `both` THEN `both`
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN `the ordinary percentage`
            ELSE `the ordinary percentage`
        `the ordinary percentage` MEANS
            IF      (`the loss`'s `the Schedule 1 item`) EQUALS 41
                AND (    `the sexual organ losses`'s `the penis is lost`
                     OR  `the sexual organ losses`'s `the number of testicles lost, an only testicle counting as 2` AT LEAST 1)
            THEN `the s 57 percentage` `the sexual organ losses`
            ELSE `the Schedule 1 percentage of item` (`the item compensated under s 54` (`the loss`'s `the Schedule 1 item`) `the worker's left arm or hand is dominant`)

-- The losses from one injury together. NOTHING if any item is not in Schedule 1.
GIVEN `the losses` IS A LIST OF `Permanent loss`
      `the worker's left arm or hand is dominant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sexual organ losses` IS A `Sexual organ losses`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the total percentage of the single loss amount for` `the losses` `the worker's left arm or hand is dominant` `the sexual organ losses` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the losses`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN JUST 0
    WHEN `first` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN
        CONSIDER `the percentage of the single loss amount for` `first` `the worker's left arm or hand is dominant` `the sexual organ losses`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST `p` THEN
            CONSIDER `the total percentage of the single loss amount for` `rest` `the worker's left arm or hand is dominant` `the sexual organ losses`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST `q` THEN JUST (`p` PLUS `q`)

-- s 53: "A worker who has suffered 2 or more losses mentioned in schedule 1 ... because of an injury is not entitled to
-- receive as compensation under this part more than the maximum loss amount for the losses."
-- READING: s 61 deductions are made loss by loss before the s 53 cap. A single loss can also exceed the cap only
-- through the s 56 reading (an only arm at or above the elbow, 155%); the cap is applied there too.
GIVEN `the losses` IS A LIST OF `Permanent loss`
      `the worker's left arm or hand is dominant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sexual organ losses` IS A `Sexual organ losses`
      `the single loss amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum loss amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the lump sum for` `the losses` `the worker's left arm or hand is dominant` `the sexual organ losses` `the single loss amount` `the maximum loss amount` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the total percentage of the single loss amount for` `the losses` `the worker's left arm or hand is dominant` `the sexual organ losses`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `p` THEN JUST (min `the maximum loss amount` (`the single loss amount` TIMES `p` DIVIDED BY 100))

§§ `121 -- when a claim for a lump sum may be made`

-- s 121(1): a claim under part 4.4 "may not be made earlier than 2 years after the injury". (2): earlier if "(a) the
-- injury is an imminently fatal asbestos-related disease [out of scope]; or (b) the injury has stabilised; or (c) in
-- any other case--the Magistrates Court allows the claim to be made". (4): taken to have stabilised if "(a) the worker
-- has returned to work for the worker's pre-incapacity weekly hours ... or longer; and (b) the worker has been working
-- at least the previous work hours for at least 3 months". (5): it "may have stabilised even if the worker has not
-- returned to work" -- a judgment, asked as a fact.
GIVEN `the worker has returned to work for the pre-incapacity weekly hours or longer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the worker has worked at least those hours for at least 3 months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury has otherwise stabilised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the injury has stabilised under s 121` `the worker has returned to work for the pre-incapacity weekly hours or longer` `the worker has worked at least those hours for at least 3 months` `the injury has otherwise stabilised` IF
        (`the worker has returned to work for the pre-incapacity weekly hours or longer` AND `the worker has worked at least those hours for at least 3 months`)
    OR  `the injury has otherwise stabilised`

DECLARE `Lump sum claim timing` IS ONE OF
    `a lump sum claim may be made now (s 121(2))`
    `a lump sum claim may not be made before` HAS `the day` IS A DATE

GIVEN `the date of the injury` IS A DATE
      `the injury has stabilised` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Magistrates Court allows an earlier claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Lump sum claim timing`
`when a lump sum claim may be made` `the date of the injury` `the injury has stabilised` `the Magistrates Court allows an earlier claim` MEANS
    IF `the injury has stabilised` OR `the Magistrates Court allows an earlier claim`
    THEN `a lump sum claim may be made now (s 121(2))`
    ELSE `a lump sum claim may not be made before` (`years after` 2 `the date of the injury`)

§§ `77 -- death benefits`

-- Dictionary: "dependant, of a dead worker, means an individual--(a) who was totally or partly dependent on the
-- worker's earnings on the day of the worker's death or who would, apart from the worker's incapacity because of the
-- injury, have been so dependent; and (b) who was--(i) a member of the worker's family; or (ii) a person to whom the
-- worker acted in place of a parent or who acted in place of a parent for the worker."
-- s 77(3): in working out whether a child was dependent on the worker's earnings, "any family tax benefit within the
-- meaning of the A New Tax System (Family Assistance) Act 1999 (Cwlth) ... must be disregarded" -- the fact is asked
-- with family tax benefit left out.
GIVEN `was totally or partly dependent on the worker's earnings, leaving out family tax benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `would have been so dependent but for the worker's incapacity from the injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a member of the worker's family` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the worker acted in place of a parent for the person, or the person for the worker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a dependant of the dead worker` `was totally or partly dependent on the worker's earnings, leaving out family tax benefit` `would have been so dependent but for the worker's incapacity from the injury` `is a member of the worker's family` `the worker acted in place of a parent for the person, or the person for the worker` IF
        (`was totally or partly dependent on the worker's earnings, leaving out family tax benefit` OR `would have been so dependent but for the worker's incapacity from the injury`)
    AND (`is a member of the worker's family` OR `the worker acted in place of a parent for the person, or the person for the worker`)

-- Dictionary: "child, of a worker, means a child of the worker who is--(a) not in a domestic partnership; and
-- (b) under16 years old or a full-time student"; "full-time student means an individual who--(a) is at least 16 years
-- old but younger than 25; and (b) is receiving full-time education at a secondary or tertiary educational
-- institution". s 77(5): the weekly payment "is payable only while the person receiving it is a child".
GIVEN `is the worker's child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is in a domestic partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `age in years` IS A NUMBER
      `is receiving full-time secondary or tertiary education` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a child of the worker for the Act` `is the worker's child` `is in a domestic partnership` `age in years` `is receiving full-time secondary or tertiary education` IF
        `is the worker's child`
    AND (NOT `is in a domestic partnership`)
    AND (    `age in years` LESS THAN 16
         OR  (`age in years` AT LEAST 16 AND `age in years` LESS THAN 25 AND `is receiving full-time secondary or tertiary education`))

-- s 77(2): "The dependants of the worker are entitled to the following: (a) a single lump sum payment of $539 002.37
-- wpi indexed to be divided between the dependants; (b) for each dependant who is a child--weekly compensation of
-- $148.23 wpi indexed; (c) the funeral expenses of the worker to a maximum of $11 828.87 cpi indexed."
-- (4): the lump sum "need not be divided equally ... but may be divided between them as the Magistrates Court
-- considers appropriate"; s 78(1): it "must be paid into the Magistrates Court, unless the court otherwise orders".
-- (6): "If the worker did not have dependants, the personal representative of the worker is entitled to a maximum of
-- $11 828.87 cpi indexed for the funeral expenses of the worker."
DECLARE `Death benefit recipients` IS ONE OF
    `the dependants: the lump sum is paid into the Magistrates Court and divided as it considers appropriate (ss 77(4), 78)`
    `the personal representative: funeral expenses only (s 77(6))`
    `no one: compensation is not payable under the Act for the death (s 77(1))`

DECLARE `Death benefits` HAS
    `paid to`                                              IS A `Death benefit recipients`
    `the lump sum to be divided between the dependants`    IS A NUMBER
    `weekly compensation for each dependent child`         IS A NUMBER
    `weekly compensation for all the dependent children`   IS A NUMBER
    `funeral expenses payable`                             IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `compensation is payable for the death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of dependants` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of dependants who are children` IS A NUMBER
      `the funeral expenses` IS A NUMBER
      `the death lump sum as indexed` IS A NUMBER
      `the weekly payment for a dependent child as indexed` IS A NUMBER
      `the funeral expenses maximum as indexed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Death benefits`
`the death benefits` `compensation is payable for the death` `the number of dependants` `the number of dependants who are children` `the funeral expenses` `the death lump sum as indexed` `the weekly payment for a dependent child as indexed` `the funeral expenses maximum as indexed` MEANS
    IF (NOT `compensation is payable for the death`)
    THEN `Death benefits` WITH
             `paid to`                                            IS `no one: compensation is not payable under the Act for the death (s 77(1))`
             `the lump sum to be divided between the dependants`  IS 0
             `weekly compensation for each dependent child`       IS 0
             `weekly compensation for all the dependent children` IS 0
             `funeral expenses payable`                           IS 0
    ELSE IF `the number of dependants` AT LEAST 1
         THEN `Death benefits` WITH
                  `paid to`                                            IS `the dependants: the lump sum is paid into the Magistrates Court and divided as it considers appropriate (ss 77(4), 78)`
                  `the lump sum to be divided between the dependants`  IS `the death lump sum as indexed`
                  `weekly compensation for each dependent child`       IS (IF `the number of dependants who are children` AT LEAST 1 THEN `the weekly payment for a dependent child as indexed` ELSE 0)
                  `weekly compensation for all the dependent children` IS `the number of dependants who are children` TIMES `the weekly payment for a dependent child as indexed`
                  `funeral expenses payable`                           IS min `the funeral expenses` `the funeral expenses maximum as indexed`
         ELSE `Death benefits` WITH
                  `paid to`                                            IS `the personal representative: funeral expenses only (s 77(6))`
                  `the lump sum to be divided between the dependants`  IS 0
                  `weekly compensation for each dependent child`       IS 0
                  `weekly compensation for all the dependent children` IS 0
                  `funeral expenses payable`                           IS min `the funeral expenses` `the funeral expenses maximum as indexed`

§§ `116-122 -- making a claim`

-- s 122(1)(b), (2): a claim (other than for an imminently fatal asbestos-related disease) "is made on the day the claim
-- is given to ... the employer or the insurer", and if given to them on different days, "on the day the claim is given
-- to the first of them".
-- s 116(2)(b): "A claim for weekly compensation must be accompanied by a medical certificate from ... a doctor."
-- s 118(2): the certificate must "(a) comply with the requirements for medical assessments prescribed by regulation
-- [not deposited: whether it complies is a fact]; and (b) include a statement of the doctor's assessment of whether
-- the worker's condition is consistent with the worker's employment being a substantial contributing factor".
-- s 119(2): if the insurer (or licensed self-insurer) tells the worker in writing about the deficiency "as soon as
-- possible (but in any case within 72 hours) after receiving the claim, the claim is not considered to have been made
-- until section 118 (2) is complied with"; (3): if it does not, "the claim is taken to comply"; (4): (2) does not
-- apply if the insurer waives the requirement.
`the hours to flag a deficient medical certificate` MEANS 72

DECLARE `Certificate answer` IS ONE OF
    `the claim complies with s 118(2)`
    `the claim is taken to comply with s 118(2) (s 119(3))`
    `the insurer waived compliance with s 118(2) (s 119(4))`
    `the claim is not made until a complying medical certificate is given (s 119(2))`

GIVEN `the claim is for weekly compensation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the medical certificate complies with s 118(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insurer told the worker in writing what was missing within 72 hours of receiving the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insurer waived the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Certificate answer`
`the medical certificate position` `the claim is for weekly compensation` `the medical certificate complies with s 118(2)` `the insurer told the worker in writing what was missing within 72 hours of receiving the claim` `the insurer waived the requirement` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the claim is for weekly compensation`) OR `the medical certificate complies with s 118(2)`
    THEN `the claim complies with s 118(2)`
    ELSE IF `the insurer waived the requirement`
         THEN `the insurer waived compliance with s 118(2) (s 119(4))`
         ELSE IF `the insurer told the worker in writing what was missing within 72 hours of receiving the claim`
              THEN `the claim is not made until a complying medical certificate is given (s 119(2))`
              ELSE `the claim is taken to comply with s 118(2) (s 119(3))`

GIVEN `the day the claim was first given to the employer or the insurer` IS A DATE
      `the certificate position` IS A `Certificate answer`
      `the day a complying medical certificate was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the claim is made under s 119 and s 122` `the day the claim was first given to the employer or the insurer` `the certificate position` `the day a complying medical certificate was given` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the certificate position`
    WHEN `the claim is not made until a complying medical certificate is given (s 119(2))` THEN `the day a complying medical certificate was given`
    OTHERWISE `the day the claim was first given to the employer or the insurer`

§§ `120 -- time for taking proceedings`

-- s 120(1): a proceeding for the recovery of compensation "may continue only if--(a) notice of the injury (an injury
-- notice) was given as soon as practicable after the injury happened, and before the worker voluntarily left the
-- employment in which the worker was injured; and (b) the claim for compensation was made--(i) within 3 years after the
-- injury happened; or (ii) if the worker was not aware of the injury when it happened--within 3 years after the worker
-- became aware of the injury; or (iii) if the worker dies--within 3 years after the claimant became aware of the
-- death." (2): it may also continue if the Magistrates Court allows it under s 120A, or under s 124 (no notice, or a
-- defective notice, that did not prejudice the employer's defence or was caused by ignorance, mistake or another
-- reasonable cause). "As soon as practicable" is a judgment, asked as a fact.
`the years to claim under s 120` MEANS 3

GIVEN `the day the 3 years run from` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to claim under s 120` `the day the 3 years run from` MEANS `years after` `the years to claim under s 120` `the day the 3 years run from`

DECLARE `Proceeding answer` IS ONE OF
    `the proceeding may continue (s 120(1))`
    `the proceeding may continue only if the Magistrates Court allows it (s 120A) or s 124 applies`

GIVEN `the injury notice was given as soon as practicable and before the worker voluntarily left the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the claim is made` IS A DATE
      `the day the 3 years run from` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Proceeding answer`
`whether a proceeding may continue` `the injury notice was given as soon as practicable and before the worker voluntarily left the employment` `the day the claim is made` `the day the 3 years run from` MEANS
    IF `the injury notice was given as soon as practicable and before the worker voluntarily left the employment`
       AND (`the day the claim is made` `is on or before` (`the last day to claim under s 120` `the day the 3 years run from`))
    THEN `the proceeding may continue (s 120(1))`
    ELSE `the proceeding may continue only if the Magistrates Court allows it (s 120A) or s 124 applies`

§§ `127-134 -- accepting and rejecting claims`

-- s 127(1): the insurer is the licensed insurer with the employer's compulsory insurance policy, or "if the employer was
-- a licensed self-insurer when the injury happened--the employer" (the DI fund cases are out of scope). (2): a claim is
-- given to the insurer if it is given to the licensed insurer or the insurer is given notice of it by the employer or
-- the worker.
-- s 128(2): "If, at the end of 28 days after the day the insurer receives the claim, the insurer has not decided to
-- reject the claim--(a) the insurer is taken to have accepted the claim; and (b) any payment made by the insurer in
-- relation to the claim is not recoverable." READING: s 128 counts from the day the insurer "receives" the claim and
-- ss 130-131 from the day it "is given to" the insurer (s 127(2)); one date stands for both.
`the days to reject before acceptance` MEANS 28

DECLARE `Acceptance answer` IS ONE OF
    `the claim is taken to be accepted at the end of` HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `the claim is not taken to be accepted: the insurer decided to reject it within 28 days`
    `acceptance not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

GIVEN `the claim is for an imminently fatal asbestos-related disease` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the insurer received the claim` IS A DATE
      `the insurer decided to reject the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the insurer decided to reject it` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Acceptance answer`
`whether the claim is taken to be accepted` `the claim is for an imminently fatal asbestos-related disease` `the day the insurer received the claim` `the insurer decided to reject the claim` `the day the insurer decided to reject it` MEANS
    IF `the claim is for an imminently fatal asbestos-related disease`
    THEN `acceptance not covered` `a claim for an imminently fatal asbestos-related disease (ss 116(2)(a), 121(2)(a), 122(1)(a), 128A) is outside this encoding`
    ELSE IF `the insurer decided to reject the claim` AND (`the day the insurer decided to reject it` `is on or before` `the end of the 28 days`)
         THEN `the claim is not taken to be accepted: the insurer decided to reject it within 28 days`
         ELSE `the claim is taken to be accepted at the end of` `the end of the 28 days`
    WHERE
        `the end of the 28 days` MEANS `days after` `the days to reject before acceptance` `the day the insurer received the claim`

-- s 129(1): "An insurer rejects a claim ... by written notice given to the worker and, unless the insurer is a licensed
-- self-insurer, the employer." (2)-(3): rejected when the notice is received by the last of them. (4): "The notice must
-- include the reason"; (5): from 28 days, "a statement explaining why"; (6): "for medical reasons" without the medical
-- reasons is taken not to contain the reason. READING: a notice without the reason (or, from 28 days, the statement) is
-- not a rejection under s 129, so it lets no payment stop.
-- s 130(1)(a): rejected "within 28 days after the claim is given to the insurer": the insurer "may--(a) stop weekly
-- compensation to the worker 2 weeks after the insurer rejects the claim". (2): not entitled to reject within 28 days
-- "only on the ground that the insurer has not had time to adequately assess the claim".
-- s 131(a): rejected "28 days or later, but not later than 1 year, after the claim is given": may "stop weekly
-- compensation to the worker 8 weeks after the insurer rejects the claim".
-- s 132(1): from 1 year "only with the leave of the Magistrates Court"; (2)(b): may stop "(i) on the day stated by the
-- court in the order giving leave ...; or (ii) 8 weeks after the worker gets notice of the rejection if no day is
-- stated"; (3): the worker gets notice on the day the court gives leave if present, otherwise on receiving the notice.
-- The boundaries overlap: a rejection on the 28th day is both "within 28 days" (s 130) and "28 days or later" (s 131),
-- and one on the first anniversary both "not later than 1 year" (s 131) and "1 year or later" (s 132). READING: the
-- earlier section applies at each boundary (s 128 supports it at 28: acceptance comes only "at the end of 28 days").
-- s 134(1): the licensed insurer "is liable to pay weekly compensation ... until the insurer rejects or settles the
-- claim"; (2) such a payment "may not be recovered by the licensed insurer".
`the days of weekly compensation after a rejection within 28 days` MEANS 14
`the days of weekly compensation after a later rejection` MEANS 56

DECLARE `Rejection timing` IS ONE OF
    `rejected within 28 days after the claim was given to the insurer (s 130)`
    `rejected 28 days or later but not later than 1 year after the claim was given to the insurer (s 131)`
    `rejected 1 year or later after the claim was given to the insurer (s 132)`

GIVEN `the claim day` IS A DATE
      `the rejection day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Rejection timing`
`the timing of the rejection` `the claim day` `the rejection day` MEANS
    IF `the rejection day` `is on or before` (`days after` `the days to reject before acceptance` `the claim day`)
    THEN `rejected within 28 days after the claim was given to the insurer (s 130)`
    ELSE IF `the rejection day` `is on or before` (`years after` 1 `the claim day`)
         THEN `rejected 28 days or later but not later than 1 year after the claim was given to the insurer (s 131)`
         ELSE `rejected 1 year or later after the claim was given to the insurer (s 132)`

DECLARE `Why weekly compensation continues` IS ONE OF
    `the notice does not give the reason for rejecting the claim (s 129(4)-(6))`
    `the only ground is that the insurer has not had time to assess the claim (s 130(2))`
    `from 1 year the insurer may reject only with the Magistrates Court's leave (s 132(1))`

DECLARE `Stop answer` IS ONE OF
    `weekly compensation may stop from` HAS `the day` IS A DATE, `under` IS A STRING
    `the rejection does not let weekly compensation stop: the insurer stays liable until it rejects or settles (s 134(1))` HAS `because` IS A `Why weekly compensation continues`

DECLARE `Rejection facts` HAS
    `the day the claim was given to the insurer`                                 IS A DATE     -- s 127(2)
    `the day the claim is taken to be rejected`                                  IS A DATE     -- s 129(2)-(3)
    `the notice gives the reason, and from 28 days a statement explaining why`   IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 129(4)-(6)
    `the only ground is that the insurer has not had time to assess the claim`   IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 130(2)
    `the Magistrates Court gave leave to reject`                                 IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 132(1)
    `the court's order states a day to stop`                                     IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 132(2)(b)(i)
    `the day stated in the order`                                                IS A DATE     -- s 132(2)(b)(i)
    `the day the worker got notice of the rejection`                             IS A DATE     -- s 132(3)

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Rejection facts`
GIVETH A `Stop answer`
`when weekly compensation may stop after a rejection` `the facts` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the facts`'s `the notice gives the reason, and from 28 days a statement explaining why`)
    THEN `the rejection does not let weekly compensation stop: the insurer stays liable until it rejects or settles (s 134(1))` `the notice does not give the reason for rejecting the claim (s 129(4)-(6))`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the timing of the rejection` (`the facts`'s `the day the claim was given to the insurer`) (`the facts`'s `the day the claim is taken to be rejected`)
         WHEN `rejected within 28 days after the claim was given to the insurer (s 130)` THEN
             IF `the facts`'s `the only ground is that the insurer has not had time to assess the claim`
             THEN `the rejection does not let weekly compensation stop: the insurer stays liable until it rejects or settles (s 134(1))` `the only ground is that the insurer has not had time to assess the claim (s 130(2))`
             ELSE `weekly compensation may stop from` (`days after` `the days of weekly compensation after a rejection within 28 days` (`the facts`'s `the day the claim is taken to be rejected`)) "s 130(1)(a)"
         WHEN `rejected 28 days or later but not later than 1 year after the claim was given to the insurer (s 131)` THEN
             `weekly compensation may stop from` (`days after` `the days of weekly compensation after a later rejection` (`the facts`'s `the day the claim is taken to be rejected`)) "s 131(a)"
         WHEN `rejected 1 year or later after the claim was given to the insurer (s 132)` THEN
             IF (NOT `the facts`'s `the Magistrates Court gave leave to reject`)
             THEN `the rejection does not let weekly compensation stop: the insurer stays liable until it rejects or settles (s 134(1))` `from 1 year the insurer may reject only with the Magistrates Court's leave (s 132(1))`
             ELSE IF `the facts`'s `the court's order states a day to stop`
                  THEN `weekly compensation may stop from` (`the facts`'s `the day stated in the order`) "s 132(2)(b)(i)"
                  ELSE `weekly compensation may stop from` (`days after` `the days of weekly compensation after a later rejection` (`the facts`'s `the day the worker got notice of the rejection`)) "s 132(2)(b)(ii)"

-- What the insurer may recover. s 128(2)(b): after acceptance by silence, "any payment made by the insurer in relation
-- to the claim is not recoverable". s 134(2): a payment of weekly compensation or costs before the insurer rejects or
-- settles "may not be recovered by the licensed insurer"; (3): but the insurer "is not liable to pay, and may recover
-- from the employer, an amount that the employer is liable to pay under section 95" (weekly compensation from the date
-- of injury until a late injury notice), which (4) does not affect for a licensed self-insurer. (s 135, refunds after a
-- Criminal Code offence, is out of scope.)
DECLARE `Recovery answer` IS ONE OF
    `the insurer may not recover it from the worker (s 128(2)(b), s 134(2))`
    `the insurer may not recover it from the worker, but may recover from the employer what the employer owes under s 95 (s 134(3))`

GIVEN `the employer gave the injury notice late, so that s 95 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insurer is a licensed self-insurer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Recovery answer`
`what the insurer may recover` `the employer gave the injury notice late, so that s 95 applies` `the insurer is a licensed self-insurer` MEANS
    IF `the employer gave the injury notice late, so that s 95 applies` AND (NOT `the insurer is a licensed self-insurer`)
    THEN `the insurer may not recover it from the worker, but may recover from the employer what the employer owes under s 95 (s 134(3))`
    ELSE `the insurer may not recover it from the worker (s 128(2)(b), s 134(2))`

§§ `93-95 -- the injury notice to the insurer`

-- s 93(1): "The injured worker must tell the employer that the worker has received a workplace injury as soon as
-- possible after being injured." (2): "The employer must give the insurer notice of the injury (an injury notice) under
-- section 94 within 48 hours after becoming aware that the worker has received a workplace injury." (3): (2) "does not
-- apply if the insurer is a licensed self-insurer".
-- s 94(2): "The employer may give the notice orally, in writing or in electronic form." (3): "if the employer gives
-- the notice orally, the employer must give the notice in writing or in electronic form within 3 days after giving the
-- notice orally." READING: on an hours clock, 3 days is 72 hours.
-- s 95(2): an employer that does not give the injury notice within that time "is liable to pay the worker weekly
-- compensation from the date of injury until the employer gives the insurer the injury notice", and (3) "must not be
-- indemnified by the insurer" for it.
`the hours to give the insurer an injury notice` MEANS 48
`the hours to confirm an oral injury notice` MEANS 72
`the days to forward a claim to the insurer` MEANS 7

DECLARE `Late notice answer` IS ONE OF
    `no extra liability: the injury notice was given within 48 hours (s 93(2))`
    `no injury notice to an insurer is required: the employer is a licensed self-insurer (s 93(3))`
    `the employer pays the weekly compensation itself, without indemnity, for the days` HAS `from` IS A DATE, `to` IS A DATE

GIVEN `the employer is a licensed self-insurer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hours from becoming aware of the injury to giving the insurer the injury notice` IS A NUMBER
      `the date of the injury` IS A DATE
      `the day the employer gave the insurer the injury notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Late notice answer`
`what a late injury notice costs the employer` `the employer is a licensed self-insurer` `the hours from becoming aware of the injury to giving the insurer the injury notice` `the date of the injury` `the day the employer gave the insurer the injury notice` MEANS
    IF `the employer is a licensed self-insurer`
    THEN `no injury notice to an insurer is required: the employer is a licensed self-insurer (s 93(3))`
    ELSE IF `the hours from becoming aware of the injury to giving the insurer the injury notice` AT MOST `the hours to give the insurer an injury notice`
         THEN `no extra liability: the injury notice was given within 48 hours (s 93(2))`
         ELSE `the employer pays the weekly compensation itself, without indemnity, for the days` `the date of the injury` `the day the employer gave the insurer the injury notice`

§§ `Regulative rules -- the worker, the employer and the insurer`

DECLARE `WCA party` IS ONE OF `the worker`, `the employer`, `the insurer`

DECLARE `Notice form` IS ONE OF `orally`, `in writing`, `in electronic form`

DECLARE `WCA act` IS ONE OF
    `tell the employer about the injury`
    `begin paying weekly compensation`
    `make a claim for compensation`
    `stop paying weekly compensation`
    `give the insurer an injury notice` HAS `form` IS A `Notice form`
    `give the injury notice in writing or in electronic form`
    `forward the claim to the insurer`
    `tell the worker in writing what the medical certificate lacks`
    `give a medical certificate that complies with s 118(2)`
    `decide to reject the claim`
    `recover a payment made on the claim`
    `make a claim for a permanent injury lump sum`
    `apply to the Magistrates Court to allow the late claim`

-- s 93(1) and s 38(1)(a), (4)-(5). Clock: days, from the injury. The worker must tell the employer "as soon as
-- possible": no number of days is set, so the obligation never falls due by time alone. Once the worker gives notice,
-- the employer must begin weekly payments "when the worker gives notice" -- READING: the same day. s 38(4): failing to
-- do so is an offence (10 penalty units), (5) of strict liability. The duty arises only if the worker "is or may be
-- entitled to compensation for a compensable injury".
`the same day` MEANS 0

GIVEN `the worker is or may be entitled to compensation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `WCA party` `WCA act`
DECIDE `s 93(1), s 38(1) -- the worker tells the employer, and the employer must then begin weekly payments` IS
    PARTY `the worker`
    MUST  `tell the employer about the injury`
    HENCE
        IF `the worker is or may be entitled to compensation`
        THEN PARTY `the employer`
             MUST  `begin paying weekly compensation`
             WITHIN `the same day`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "s 38(1)(a), (4): the employer must begin weekly compensation when the worker gives notice of the injury; failing to is a strict liability offence, maximum 10 penalty units"
        ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 38(2)-(3). Clock: days, from the injury (or, under s 38(3), the days run to 7 days after the worker is first able
-- to claim; the seat works out the number). The worker MAY claim (s 116(1)); not claiming is no breach, but if no claim
-- is made in time, "payment of weekly compensation ends": the employer may stop paying.
GIVEN `the days the worker has to claim` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `WCA party` `WCA act`
DECIDE `s 38(2), (3) -- a claim within 7 days keeps weekly payments going, or they may stop` IS
    PARTY `the worker`
    DO    `make a claim for compensation`
    WITHIN `the days the worker has to claim`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST
        PARTY `the employer`
        MAY   `stop paying weekly compensation`

-- s 93(2)-(3), s 94(2)-(3), s 95. Clock: hours, from the employer becoming aware of the workplace injury.
GIVEN `the employer is a licensed self-insurer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `WCA party` `WCA act`
DECIDE `s 93(2), s 94(3) -- the employer must give the insurer an injury notice within 48 hours, and confirm an oral one within 3 days` IS
    IF `the employer is a licensed self-insurer`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the employer`
         MUST  `give the insurer an injury notice` `how`
         WITHIN `the hours to give the insurer an injury notice`
         HENCE
             CONSIDER `how`
             WHEN `orally` THEN
                 PARTY `the employer`
                 MUST  `give the injury notice in writing or in electronic form`
                 WITHIN `the hours to confirm an oral injury notice`
                 LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "s 94(3): an injury notice given orally must be given in writing or in electronic form within 3 days"
             OTHERWISE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "s 93(2), s 95: the employer must give the insurer an injury notice within 48 hours of becoming aware of the injury; if it does not, it must pay the worker's weekly compensation from the date of injury until it does, without indemnity from the insurer"

-- s 126(1), (4)-(5). Clock: days, from the employer receiving the claim. "the employer must, within 7 days after the day
-- the employer receives the claim or document, forward it to the liable insurer" (50 penalty units, strict liability);
-- not for a licensed self-insurer.
GIVEN `the employer is a licensed self-insurer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `WCA party` `WCA act`
DECIDE `s 126(1) -- the employer must forward the claim to the insurer within 7 days` IS
    IF `the employer is a licensed self-insurer`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the employer`
         MUST  `forward the claim to the insurer`
         WITHIN `the days to forward a claim to the insurer`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "s 126(1): the employer must forward a claim to the liable insurer within 7 days of receiving it; failing to is a strict liability offence, maximum 50 penalty units"

-- s 119. Clock: hours, from the insurer receiving the claim. Flagging the deficiency is the insurer's choice (DO), not a
-- duty: if it does so within 72 hours, the claim is made only when the worker gives a complying certificate; if not,
-- the claim is taken to comply (LEST FULFILLED).
GIVEN `the medical certificate complies with s 118(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insurer waived the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `WCA party` `WCA act`
DECIDE `s 119 -- a deficient medical certificate must be flagged within 72 hours, or the claim is taken to comply` IS
    IF `the medical certificate complies with s 118(2)` OR `the insurer waived the requirement`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the insurer`
         DO    `tell the worker in writing what the medical certificate lacks`
         WITHIN `the hours to flag a deficient medical certificate`
         HENCE (PARTY `the worker` DO `give a medical certificate that complies with s 118(2)`)
         LEST  FULFILLED

-- s 128(2). Clock: days, from the insurer receiving the claim. Deciding to reject is the insurer's choice (DO); if 28
-- days pass without it, the insurer is taken to have accepted, and must not recover what it paid on the claim. (Under
-- s 134(2) payments before rejection are not recoverable either way; that is in `what the insurer may recover`.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `WCA party` `WCA act`
DECIDE `s 128 -- the insurer is taken to accept a claim it has not decided to reject within 28 days` IS
    PARTY `the insurer`
    DO    `decide to reject the claim`
    WITHIN `the days to reject before acceptance`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST
        PARTY `the insurer`
        SHANT `recover a payment made on the claim`
        LEST  BREACH BY `the insurer` BECAUSE "s 128(2): the insurer did not decide to reject the claim within 28 days, so it is taken to have accepted it, and a payment made on the claim is not recoverable"

-- ss 130-132, 134(1). Clock: days, from the day the claim is taken to be rejected (or, for s 132(2)(b)(ii), from the day
-- the worker got notice). The insurer must not stop weekly compensation before the day it may stop; the seat works out
-- that day with `when weekly compensation may stop after a rejection`, and the number of days to it is the parameter.
-- On the day itself stopping is allowed, so the prohibition runs to the day before (WITHIN the days less 1).
-- Where the rejection lets nothing stop, the prohibition has no end date: s 134(1) keeps the insurer liable "until the
-- insurer rejects or settles the claim".
GIVEN `the stop answer` IS A `Stop answer`
      `the days from the rejection to the day weekly compensation may stop` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `WCA party` `WCA act`
DECIDE `ss 130-132, 134 -- after a rejection, the insurer must keep paying weekly compensation until the day it may stop` IS
    CONSIDER `the stop answer`
    WHEN `weekly compensation may stop from` `the day` `under` THEN
        PARTY `the insurer`
        SHANT `stop paying weekly compensation`
        WITHIN (`the days from the rejection to the day weekly compensation may stop` MINUS 1)
        LEST  BREACH BY `the insurer` BECAUSE "ss 130-132, 134(1): the insurer stopped weekly compensation before the day the Act lets it stop after rejecting the claim"
    WHEN `the rejection does not let weekly compensation stop: the insurer stays liable until it rejects or settles (s 134(1))` `why` THEN
        PARTY `the insurer`
        SHANT `stop paying weekly compensation`
        LEST  BREACH BY `the insurer` BECAUSE "s 134(1): the rejection does not take effect, so the insurer stays liable to pay weekly compensation until it rejects or settles the claim"

-- s 120(1)(b). Clock: days, from the day the 3 years run from (the injury, the worker's awareness of it, or the
-- claimant's awareness of the death); the seat works out the number of days. Claiming is the worker's choice (DO). If
-- the 3 years pass, the proceeding may continue only if the Magistrates Court allows it (s 120A) or s 124 applies.
GIVEN `the days in the 3 years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `WCA party` `WCA act`
DECIDE `s 120 -- the claim is made within 3 years, or only the Magistrates Court can let the proceeding continue` IS
    PARTY `the worker`
    DO    `make a claim for compensation`
    WITHIN `the days in the 3 years`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST
        PARTY `the worker`
        MAY   `apply to the Magistrates Court to allow the late claim`

-- s 121. Clock: days, from the injury; the seat works out the days to the second anniversary. A part 4.4 claim "may not
-- be made earlier than 2 years after the injury", unless the injury has stabilised or the Magistrates Court allows it.
-- A claim on the anniversary itself is in time, so the prohibition runs to the day before.
GIVEN `the days to the second anniversary of the injury` IS A NUMBER
      `the injury has stabilised` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Magistrates Court allows an earlier claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `WCA party` `WCA act`
DECIDE `s 121 -- no permanent injury claim earlier than 2 years after the injury, unless it has stabilised or the court allows` IS
    IF `the injury has stabilised` OR `the Magistrates Court allows an earlier claim`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the worker`
         SHANT `make a claim for a permanent injury lump sum`
         WITHIN (`the days to the second anniversary of the injury` MINUS 1)
         LEST  BREACH BY `the worker` BECAUSE "s 121(1): a claim under part 4.4 may not be made earlier than 2 years after the injury unless the injury has stabilised or the Magistrates Court allows it"
